tollgate (#84): client_secret in JSON keeps the closing quote, the comma and the
rest of a compact object; only the value is replaced. Rust rewrites the prefix
and replaces everything up to the next whitespace.
-- input --
{"client_secret": "S3cretPwd!Long", "id": 1}
{"client_secret":"S3cretPwd!Long","id":1}
-- must_contain --
"id": 1}
"id":1}
-- must_not_contain --
S3cretPwd
-- want --
{"client_secret": "<redacted:api_key>", "id": 1}
{"client_secret":"<redacted:api_key>","id":1}
-- deviation --
prefix
